colleagues peers  is that it runs pretty  was a little deep in 1989 ray texal won  the two most prestigious middle finals  in the u.s he's a well-known trainer  he's at the top level of his sport and  he also feels as though safe sport has  been operating like a secret court  the feeling of it is you don't know  what's going on this is not falling in  the criminal justice system or the  justice system  it's a step towards it and i think that  that's where a lot of the division comes  from is  not wanting to support something of that  nature that's operating in that way  but at the same time supporting its  message  and and its purpose  and there's a conflict there  people in my community afraid of related  to safe sport is  very specifically the use of c sport  as a weapon  whether that's for retribution  whether that's displeasure with somebody  of course that's a very scary  proposition  so my early thoughts of safe sport were  definitely influenced by the people  around me  and a lot of people were trainers  i heard things you know like say sports  a witch hunt these are innocent trainers  not doing anything and  if clients don't like them they can go  after them for absolutely anything  i never really understood what safe  sport was until i actually needed to go  through with it  um and it's a lot different from what  people think  i kind of was like i'm just gonna make a  social media post it's gonna be over  gonna keep moving on and then so many  women started reaching out to me so many  women and men of all ages talking about  their stories  and i was like okay wait i'm not the  only one this is a huge problem in our  industry that is not talked about enough  um all it's talked about is how safe  sports a witch hunt and how  safe sports awful and how we need to get  rid of it and how you know how could  this be put in place  and i think a lot of times some people  forget that i'm still like an 18 year  old girl who's  coming out of the situation it's not  like it's 10 years behind me it's still  fairly close  [Music]  one of the things that the equestrian  community has struggled with is that  it's seen some of the most prestigious  trainers athletes and olympic champions  brought down by safe sport  one thing i've definitely come to  realize over the course of this  reporting is that this is a sport that  doesn't like to watch its heroes fall  for me safe sport became the most  polarizing when  the  person i think in our community that we  all looked to  the most the one with the biggest voice  george morris my former mentor and  trainer when he was set down i think  that was really maybe one of the more  significant moments when it really hit  hard for many people that this was real  and serious  when george morris was removed from  sport i don't think that anyone inside  of state sport could have predicted the  just emotional  like outcry of of that decision um it  was something that we had never seen  before the i stand with george hashtag  was was circulating and people were just  really just angry with the center  because this was someone who had been in  this community for decades he was still  coaching he was a pillar with his  community this guy had his own action  figures like this was someone that they  really looked up to and so for him to be  called out like this for him to be  removed people were just angry  within 48 hours of the george morris ban  a group called i stand with george have  popped up on facebook and it had more  than 4 200 members  they sent angry emails to safe sport  they called the center they did  everything they could  to demand his reinstatement  they didn't believe that george morris  should be brought down by allegations  dating back to the 1970s  they want to know why and how safe sport  can operate outside and beyond the scope  of the criminal justice system not  having a statute of limitations in place  allowed people to one  take their time to come to the center  for state sport